<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <AvaloniaVersion>12.1.4</AvaloniaVersion>
    <!-- The DataGrid has a repository and a release cycle of its own
         (github.com/AvaloniaUI/Avalonia.Controls.DataGrid). Up to Avalonia 11.3.13 and 12.0.0 it was still released
         with every Avalonia version under the same number; since then only when the DataGrid itself changes, and its
         numbers no longer match Avalonia's: DataGrid 12.1.2 came out a month before Avalonia 12.1.2 and has nothing
         to do with it, and there is no 12.1.3 or 12.1.4. Its dependency is a lower bound only - 12.1.2 asks for
         Avalonia 12.1.0 or later - so it goes with any 12.1.x and an Avalonia update never forces a DataGrid update.
         The other way round it can: DataGrid 12.0.1 asked for Avalonia 12.0.5. Check
         https://www.nuget.org/packages/Avalonia.Controls.DataGrid when Avalonia is updated. -->
    <AvaloniaDataGridVersion>12.1.2</AvaloniaDataGridVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
